                        details: `<p>Dawkins explicitly rejects the idea that genes rigidly control our behavior. Genes provide tendencies, leanings, and a starting point. The analogy is a recipe, not a blueprint\u2014the outcome depends on the ingredients and the oven. Environment, culture, and personal choice all play massive roles.</p>
                        <p>A common criticism is that Dawkins promotes "genetic determinism"\u2014the idea that your genes control everything. He explicitly rejects this. Genes are like a recipe, not a blueprint. A recipe provides instructions, but the outcome depends on the cook, the ingredients, and the oven temperature.</p>
                        <p>Your genes give you tendencies and predispositions. But your environment, upbringing, culture, and conscious choices shape how those tendencies are expressed. Understanding your genetic leanings gives you <em>more</em> power over them, not less.</p>`
