                        <p>Your brain receives a constant stream of noisy, incomplete, low-resolution data from your senses. But your experience of the world feels smooth, vivid, and seamless. How? Because your brain is an incredibly aggressive editor. It fills in blind spots, stabilizes shaky visual input, and <strong>constructs</strong> a coherent "movie" of reality in real-time.</p>
