                        <p>Color is not a property of the physical world. Out there, there are only electromagnetic waves of different wavelengths. "Red" is just a wavelength of about 700 nanometers. Your brain <strong>invents</strong> the experience of redness as a useful label to help you distinguish ripe fruit from unripe, or poisonous berries from safe ones.</p>
