                        <p>Eagleman uses a powerful metaphor: you think you are the Captain of the S.S. You, standing on the bridge, steering the ship. In reality, you are a stowaway on a massive ocean liner. The engines, navigation, repairs, and most decisions are all handled by a vast crew (your unconscious processes) that you never see and can't directly control.</p>
