                        <p>Your brain is not a single, unified entity. It is more like a <strong>parliament</strong> of competing factions, each with its own agenda. Your limbic system (the "emotional" brain) screams for immediate pleasure—eat the cake, scroll social media, stay in bed. Your prefrontal cortex (the "rational" brain) argues for long-term goals—stick to the diet, finish the project, get up early.</p>
