                        title: 'Shutting Down the Future',
                        body: 'Cortisol\'s job is to suppress expensive long-term projects. The immune system is a prime target\u2014chronically high cortisol keeps it in a state of suppression, making you more susceptible to colds, flu, and worse. Growth and reproduction are also suppressed. In children under severe stress, physical growth can literally be stunted\u2014a condition called "stress dwarfism."',
                        prompt: "THE HIDDEN COSTS",
                        image: 'images/zebras/3_4.png',
                        details: `<p>Cortisol\'s job is to suppress expensive long-term projects. The immune system is a prime target\u2014chronically high cortisol keeps it in a state of suppression, making you more susceptible to colds, flu, and worse. Growth and reproduction are also suppressed. In children under severe stress, physical growth can literally be stunted\u2014a condition called "stress dwarfism."</p>
                        <p>Cortisol's job is to suppress expensive, long-term biological projects, and the <strong>immune system</strong> is a prime target. While short-term stress can actually enhance immune function (preparing for a wound), chronic stress does the opposite. Chronically high cortisol keeps your immune system in a state of suppression, making you more susceptible to infectious diseases like the common cold and flu.</p>
                        <p>Growth and reproduction are also sacrificed. In adults, chronic stress can lead to decreased libido, erectile dysfunction, and fertility problems. In children suffering from severe, prolonged stress, it can lead to a condition known as <strong>"stress dwarfism"</strong>\u2014where physical growth is literally stunted because the body has decided this is no time to invest in long-term building projects.</p>`
