                        eyebrow: 'THE UNIFYING LESSON',
                        title: 'You Are Not Helpless',
                        body: 'The ultimate lesson: while you can\'t always change the stressors in your life, you have significant power to change your response to them. It\'s not the event itself, but your psychological interpretation and social context that determine its biological impact. Unlike the zebra, your complex brain gives you the tools to understand the mismatch and do something about it.',
                        prompt: "THE BOTTOM LINE",
                        image: 'images/zebras/4_4.png',
                        details: `<p>The ultimate lesson: while you can\'t always change the stressors in your life, you have significant power to change your response to them. It\'s not the event itself, but your psychological interpretation and social context that determine its biological impact. Unlike the zebra, your complex brain gives you the tools to understand the mismatch and do something about it.</p>
                        <p>The ultimate lesson of the book is both sobering and empowering. For humans, the stress response is all about the <strong>loss of control, predictability, and social support</strong>. We are a species that evolved for a certain world, and our modern lives constantly challenge our ancient coping mechanisms.</p>
                        <p>But unlike the zebra, our complex brains give us the tools to understand this mismatch and do something about it. You can seek control, build social connections, exercise, and reframe your stressors. You can use your System 2 to override your System 1's panic. You can understand your ancient programming and choose a different response. <strong>Knowledge of the mismatch is the first step to closing it.</strong></p>`
