                        prompt: "NATURE VIA NURTURE",
                        image: 'images/behave/3_3.png',
                        details: `<p>Genes don\'t determine\u2014they predispose. The same gene variant linked to antisocial behavior has virtually no effect in people who had a safe childhood; it only increases risk in those who suffered severe abuse. Genes are "if-then" clauses. And the womb is the first environment: a stressed mother\'s cortisol crosses the placenta, telling the fetal brain "the world is dangerous" and wiring it for anxiety before birth.</p>
                        <p>This connects directly to The Selfish Gene. Our genes provide the initial instructions, but Sapolsky provides a crucial modern correction: <strong>genes don't determine, they predispose</strong>. There is no gene "for" aggression or "for" compassion. Genes work in combinations and create probabilities. The classic example: a variant of the MAO-A gene associated with antisocial behavior has virtually no effect in people with a safe childhood. It only increases risk in those who also suffered severe abuse. Genes are <strong>"if-then" clauses</strong>.</p>
                        <p>The womb is the first environment. A mother experiencing chronic stress sends cortisol across the placental barrier, telling the fetal brain, "The world you're about to enter is dangerous." The brain adapts: bigger amygdala, weaker stress off-switch. The baby is born already biologically biased towards anxiety.</p>`
