                        body: 'After hundreds of pages detailing the forces that constrain us, Sapolsky\'s final message is profound optimism. Because biology is not rigidly deterministic and brains are plastic, change is always possible. Cultural norms change over centuries. Trauma can be healed. And the very fact that you can understand these influences is the first and most critical step in counteracting them.',
                        prompt: "THE HOPE",
                        image: 'images/behave/4_2.png',
                        details: `<p>After hundreds of pages detailing the forces that constrain us, Sapolsky\'s final message is profound optimism. Because biology is not rigidly deterministic and brains are plastic, change is always possible. Cultural norms change over centuries. Trauma can be healed. And the very fact that you can understand these influences is the first and most critical step in counteracting them.</p>
                        <p>After hundreds of pages detailing all the powerful biological forces that constrain us, Sapolsky's final message is one of <strong>profound optimism</strong>. Because our biology is not rigidly deterministic, and because our brains are plastic, change is possible at every level.</p>
                        <p>Deep-seated cultural norms can change over centuries. Trauma can be healed and brains rewired through therapy and new experiences. The very fact that we can <em>understand</em> these influences\u2014that we can see how our amygdala is being primed or how a cultural bias is affecting us\u2014is the first and most critical step in counteracting them. Change happens when our conscious, reflective System 2 does the <strong>"harder thing"</strong> to retrain our automatic System 1.</p>`
