                        title: 'Replace Blame with Understanding',
                        body: 'Any action you take\u2014especially one you regret\u2014is not the result of a simple "you" making a "bad decision." It is the end product of your brain chemistry, unconscious triggers, hormonal state, decades of brain plasticity, childhood experiences, genes, ancestral culture, and millions of years of primate evolution. This doesn\'t remove responsibility\u2014it replaces simplistic blame with compassionate understanding.',
                        prompt: "UNDERSTAND YOURSELF",
                        image: 'images/behave/5_1.png',
                        details: `<p>Any action you take\u2014especially one you regret\u2014is not the result of a simple "you" making a "bad decision." It is the end product of your brain chemistry, unconscious triggers, hormonal state, decades of brain plasticity, childhood experiences, genes, ancestral culture, and millions of years of primate evolution. This doesn\'t remove responsibility\u2014it replaces simplistic blame with compassionate understanding.</p>
                        <p>Behave demonstrates that any single action you take is not the result of a simple, singular "you" making a "bad decision." It is the end product of a <strong>cascade of a thousand causes</strong>: your brain chemistry in that second, the unconscious environmental triggers, your hormonal state, the brain plasticity of your last few decades, the lessons of your childhood, the genes you were dealt, the culture of your ancestors, and millions of years of primate evolution.</p>
                        <p>This is a powerful antidote to harsh self-criticism. It doesn't remove responsibility, but it replaces simplistic self-blame with a more nuanced and <strong>compassionate understanding</strong>. It allows you to say, "Given all those factors, it's understandable why that happened. Now, what are the factors I <em>can</em> change for next time?"</p>`
